# No em dashes

Do not use the em dash character (`—`, U+2014) anywhere in this repo: user-facing copy, metadata, alt text, comments, or docs.

## Prefer

- Periods for a new clause: `Indoor Dynamic sauna. Rare in Lake Arrowhead.`
- Commas for asides: `Beach clubs excluded, we say so upfront.`
- Colons for labels or lists: `Christmas Ready: $249`
- Hyphens (`-`) only for true compounds or numeric ranges: `90-minute drive`, `Dec 15-26`
- Pipes for title templates: `Shoreline rights | Lake Arrowhead A-Frame`

## Examples

```text
❌ Guest Favorite A-frame — indoor sauna, hot tub in the pines
✅ Guest Favorite A-frame. Indoor sauna, hot tub in the pines

❌ What you can — and cannot — do on the lake.
✅ What you can, and cannot, do on the lake.

❌ SEO Measurement — lakearrowheadaframe.com
✅ SEO Measurement | lakearrowheadaframe.com
```

If you find an existing em dash while editing, replace it in the same change.
